# Genuinely blocked upstream, not a "didn't get to it yet" list. Every CVE below is in a
# statically-linked Go binary already at its latest available release (or, for osv-scanner,
# pinned one version below latest for a real, documented, unrelated reason -- see
# OSV_SCANNER_VERSION's own comment in the Dockerfile). ignore-unfixed doesn't catch these because
# trivy considers the underlying Go MODULE fixed, even though the consuming binary hasn't picked
# up that fix (or, for osv-scanner, can't be bumped to the version that would without breaking
# repo_scan.py's real --local-db-path usage). Re-check whenever bumping gh/TYPESCRIPT_VERSION, or
# when repo_scan.py's osv-scanner invocation gets migrated off --local-db-path -- drop whichever
# lines a new release/migration actually fixes. Many CVEs below recur across gh, tsc, and
# osv-scanner: same underlying Go stdlib/module issue, several statically-linked binaries.

# gh CLI 2.99.0 -- unverified whether this release actually still carries these two (its
# changelog doesn't call out the fix); left in defensively rather than assumed fixed. If the next
# scan shows them clean, drop these two lines.
CVE-2026-56864
CVE-2026-56865

